title: Act1_EveWorldbuilding_P1N2
---
<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve confused>>
Eve: You really aren’t from around here?

<<set_portrait YarnManager Cyrus default>>
Cyrus: I’m not sure where I’m from.

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve confused>>
Eve: So you have the skills of a Hunter but remember nothing? Maybe you exchanged your Fates away?

<<set_portrait YarnManager Cyrus surprisedQuestionmark>>
Cyrus: Fates?

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve default>>
Eve: Strong memories, the kind that only happens a few times in a person’s life.
Eve: Depending on the memory and what Arcana it’s aligned with, they’ll grant you a unique power.
<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve oh>>
Eve: ...You at least know what an Arcana is, right?

<<set_portrait YarnManager Cyrus default>>
Cyrus: Uh. I remember, uh, Justice?

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve default>>
Eve: Eh, better than nothing.
Eve: Hmm, say you became a judge to ensure fair rulings in court. That memory might become a Fate tied to the Justice Arcana, which may grant you stronger defense.
Eve: Throughout life, we gain Fates from different Arcanas. 
Eve: Think of Arcanas as higher dimensional gods that enforce a particular belief no matter what. Together, they maintain balance in this world.
Eve: You can trade Fates like any other currency, but if you lose them all, you’ll become one of those things we ran into.
<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve defaultTalk>>
Eve: They didn’t make the warmest welcome, but luckily we have Hunters to fight them off.
Eve: I’m surprised you aren’t one already. You can make a lot of money hunting those things.

<<set_portrait YarnManager Cyrus default>>
Cyrus: [i]Hunting...the Judge mentioned something about it.[/i]
Cyrus: How do I start?

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve happyTalk>>
Eve: Guess money’s a big motivator, huh?
<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve defaultTalk>>
Eve: You'll need a dispatcher to guide you remotely. The outskirts is a distorted space, and it's constantly changing. 
<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve happyTalk>>
Eve: You'll get lost if you don't have a trained dispatcher. There's not many free around town, so you ought to choose me as your dispatcher.

<<set_portrait YarnManager Cyrus surprised>>
Cyrus: You sound eager.

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve happy>>
Eve: Our town would be a lot safer with a Hunter like you.
<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve happyEyeclosedTalk>>
Eve: Aaaand I’ll get a cut of your profits, of course.

<<set_portrait YarnManager Cyrus defaultSpeak>>
Cyrus: So [i]that's[/i] your motive.

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve happyTalk>>
Eve: Haha, yep~ You’ll need better equipment if you want to survive your first day. The shop’s up ahead.
===


