title: Act1_SliceofLife_P1N6
---
<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve happyTalk>>
Eve: Hey Dad, we’re back! Do you need help with anything?

<<set_portrait YarnManager Shopkeeper smile>>
Shopkeeper: I’m all good for now. And actually...
Shopkeeper: One of the Hunters you helped last week dropped by earlier and left a movie as thanks.

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve happyTalk >>
Eve: Oh, really? Thanks, Dad! And tell him I said thank you!

<<set_portrait YarnManager Cyrus default>>
Cyrus: You like watching movies?

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve shy >>
Eve: Psh, I’m not a full-on cinephile or anything. It’s just something I like to do when I don’t have much else going on.

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve happyTalk >>
Eve: Actually, want to come to my room and see my collection?

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve shy >>
Eve: Welcome to my room! It’s a little messy, aha...

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve oh >>
Eve: Anyhow, let’s see what this is.

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve shock >>
Eve: Oooh, it’s a new Heartline Pictures movie!
Eve: It’s called “Fatefully Yours in Lumas.”

<<clear_portrait YarnManager>>
: [i]The description says: “Margaret, an ambitious city memory-writer, returns to her hometown of Lumas to help her family’s struggling shop.[/i]
: [i]But when she meets Krys, a charming Hunter with a tragic past, she must choose between the life she built in the city and the love waiting for her at home.”[/i]

<<set_portrait YarnManager Cyrus disgust>>
Cyrus: ...Sounds pretty cheesy.

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve angry>>
Eve: Hey, don’t judge my taste in movies! Romcoms are perfectly good movies in their own right!
Eve: The lighthearted comedy paired with the heart-melting romantic elements make them both funny and sweet to watch,
Eve: and the less complex story with lower stakes makes it so you can easily watch them together with your friends and family and have fun! And ALSO-

<<set_portrait YarnManager Cyrus smug>>
Cyrus: For someone who claims to not be a movie-lover, you sure have a lot to say about them.

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve shy>>
Eve: Ehehehe...

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve happyTalk>>
Eve: Anyhow, want to watch a movie with me? There's no mission right now.

<<set_portrait YarnManager Cyrus default>>
Cyrus: Why not?

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve oh>>
Eve: On a scale of 1-10, how much of a movie watcher are you?

<<set_portrait YarnManager Cyrus surprisedSpeak >>
Cyrus: Uhhh, well, I kinda lost my memories. So a zero?

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve shock >>
Eve: What??? You don’t remember watching a single movie???

<<set_portrait YarnManager Cyrus default >>
Cyrus: Nope.

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve happy >>
Eve: Well we need to fix that right now! Since you’re new, I’ll show you one of my favorites! It’s a relaxing one.

<<clear_portrait YarnManager>>
: [i]The movie opens on a small apartment at dawn.[/i]
: [i]A young man, Ren, is trying to get his little sister ready for school while packing breakfast, sorting bills, and answering a call from work.[/i]
: [i]He burns toast, steps on a toy, and insists everything is “completely under control” while the smoke alarm goes off.[/i]
: [i]On the way to school, his sister complains about her hair. Ren tries to fix it, makes it worse...[/i]
: [i]...then offers to buy her a “good morning memory” from a kiosk to make up for it.[/i]

<<set_portrait YarnManager Cyrus surprised >>
Cyrus: That’s a thing?

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve happy >>
Eve: Small memories, mostly. Mood boosters. People buy confidence before interviews, calming memories before exams...
Eve: There are even first-date packages, which are apparently terrible.

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve defaultTalk>>
Eve: I’ve never bought one. Obviously.

<<set_portrait YarnManager Cyrus lookAway>>
Cyrus: I didn’t say anything.

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve happyEyeclosedTalk>>
Eve: Good, because if I did, I’d at least buy the premium version.

<<clear_portrait YarnManager>>
: [i]Ren sees the price and quietly puts his wallet away. Instead, he tells his sister a ridiculous story about a heroic pigeon stealing the mayor’s sandwich.[/i]
: [i]She laughs and forgets she was upset.[/i]

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve sadHappy>>
Eve: Ren’s basically raising her alone. That’s why he worries over tiny things. Kinda like dad.
Eve: He acts relaxed, but he notices everything. If I cough once, he asks if I need medicine. If I’m five minutes late, he “just happens” to be outside.

<<set_portrait YarnManager Cyrus default>>
Cyrus: He must care about you a lot.

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve sad>>
Eve: He does. Sometimes I think he cares so much because he already lost too much.
Eve: When someone is all you have left, maybe you stop asking questions that might take them away.

<<set_portrait YarnManager Cyrus lookAway>>
Cyrus: ...

<<clear_portrait YarnManager>>
: [i]On-screen, Ren’s sister auditions for a school commercial.[/i]
: [i]The teacher says they want “authentic childhood joy,” then hands the children a list of approved expressions and memories to rehearse.[/i]

<<set_portrait YarnManager Cyrus surprised>>
Cyrus: Even commercials use planted memories?

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve default>>
Eve: Of course. Manufactured celebrities are all memory design. Agencies decide what people should remember about you.

<<set_portrait YarnManager Cyrus defaultSpeak>>
Cyrus: What about Hunters?

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve oh>>
Eve: Definitely. If you became an agency Hunter, they’d probably make you the “silent protector of the forgotten city.” Lots of shots of you standing in the rain.

<<set_portrait YarnManager Cyrus disgustQuestionmark>>
Cyrus: That sounds inconvenient.

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve confused>>
Eve: That’s your reaction?

<<set_portrait YarnManager Cyrus disgust>>
Cyrus: I don’t like standing in the rain.

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve oh>>
Eve: Wow. The legend collapses immediately.

<<set_portrait YarnManager Cyrus default>>
Cyrus: Could rivals sabotage that?

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve defaultTalk>>
Eve: All the time. Leak the wrong memory, pay witnesses to remember you badly, make people associate you with cowardice or cruelty.
Eve: If enough people remember a version of you, it starts to matter more than what actually happened.

<<clear_portrait YarnManager>>
: [i]In the movie, Ren’s sister refuses the commercial because she doesn’t want strangers told how to love her.[/i]
: [i]She says she’d rather be remembered properly by her brother.[/i]

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve happyTalk>>
Eve: This is one of my favorite scenes. Being loved by one person can still count, even if the whole world doesn’t know you.

<<clear_portrait YarnManager>>
: [i]Later, Ren takes a second job delivering memory cartridges and misses his sister’s recital. He arrives just as it ends.[/i]
: [i]Instead of making excuses, he apologizes, and they sit outside eating convenience-store buns.[/i]

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve happyTalk>>
Eve: That’s what I like about family stories. Even when people mess up, there’s still this understanding underneath it.

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve sadHappy>>
Eve: I was awkward with Dad. I wanted to help with everything, but I was terrible at it. Once I tried to make breakfast and somehow made poison.

<<set_portrait YarnManager Cyrus surprised>>
Cyrus: That’s... impressive.

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve shy>>
Eve: Another time, I was taking orders and wrote down everything the client said. Including “uh,” “actually,” and “wait, no, not that one.”

<<set_portrait YarnManager Cyrus smile>>
Cyrus: At least you were thorough.

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve shy>>
Eve: Dad laughed so hard he had to go into the back room. I was furious for three days.

<<set_portrait YarnManager Cyrus surprised>>
Cyrus: Only three?

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve happyEyeclosed>>
Eve: What can I say? I’m very forgiving.

<<clear_portrait YarnManager>>
: [i]The movie ends with Ren and his sister in a slightly better apartment. He makes breakfast without burning it.[/i]
: [i]When she asks if they’ll be okay, he says, “As long as we’re together.”[/i]
: [i]The screen fades out.[/i]

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve defaultTalk>>
Eve: So? How was it?

<<set_portrait YarnManager Cyrus default>>
Cyrus: Simple, but not shallow. The ending is a little unrealistic, though. People don’t always get rewarded for trying hard.

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve happy>>
Eve: That’s fair. But sometimes I want a story to be kinder than reality. A happily ever after.

<<clear_portrait YarnManager>>
: [i]Eve’s device dings.[/i]

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve shock>>
Eve: Perfect timing! Your first mission’s already here! Let’s head out.
===


title: Act1_TownProtection_PreCombat_P1N8
---
<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve sad>>
Eve: I should’ve warned you about Dad. He’s always been overprotective, but ever since the Assimilation started picking up...

<<set_portrait YarnManager Cyrus surprised>>
Cyrus: [i]The Assimilation. The Judge mentioned that.[/i]

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve oh>>
Eve: Oh, right, you don’t know.
<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve defaultTalk>>
Eve: Once the Meminiscors have consumed enough memories, the Assimilation ritual will begin, and humanity’s memories will be completely swallowed up.
<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve sad>>
Eve: We’ve always known it would happen one day, but it’ll be sooner than we thought.

<<set_portrait YarnManager Cyrus lookAway>>
Cyrus: So the world is facing inevitable destruction? Sounds terrible.

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve sadHappy>>
Eve: Not the best place to wake up in, huh?

<<set_portrait YarnManager Cyrus default>>
Cyrus: What about the other Arcanas, then? If they preside over this world, shouldn’t they do something about its destruction?

<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve default>>
Eve: They’re not saviors or destroyers; they only seek to enforce their principles. They can’t even interfere directly with this world.
Eve: But you’re right. Perhaps certain Arcanas have already directed their followers to oppose it.
<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve defaultTalk>>
Eve: By the way, Cyrus. If you don’t mind me asking, why did you decide to become a hunter?
<<set_portrait YarnManager Cyrus default>>
Cyrus: ...
<<set_portrait YarnManager Cyrus default>>
Cyrus: Didn’t we already go over this? It’s for the money. I kind of woke up with nothing.
<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve shy>>
Eve: Oh, yeah, that’s true. 
<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve angry>>
Eve: I’m picking up memory monsters up ahead. There’s been a lot more around here lately.
<<set_portrait YarnManager Eve defaultTalk>>
Eve: I’ll guide you through. Don’t get yourself killed on your first run, okay?

<<set_portrait YarnManager Cyrus angry>>
Cyrus: I’ll try my best.
===


